# Sweep result snapshots: the CSVs are regenerable from wandb by each sweep's own
# build_dataset.py, so they stay out of the tree -- but the README (protocol, results
# table, caveats) and the regeneration script are the analysis, and do belong in it.
# Note the shape: `experiments/` alone would exclude the directory, and git never
# descends into an excluded directory, so no `!` rule beneath it could take effect.
# Excluding the *contents* and re-including the directories is what makes that work.
experiments/**
!experiments/**/
!experiments/*/README.md
!experiments/*/build_dataset.py
# MuJoCo writes this next to whatever ran; not a *.log so the rule above misses it
MUJOCO_LOG.TXT

# Credentials. fleet.sh sources ./.env if present, and a WANDB_API_KEY or HF_TOKEN
# committed here would stay in the history after any later deletion.
.env
.env.*
